<</Title (data:text/html;charset=utf-8,<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset%3D"utf-8"><style>body%7Bfont-family%3AArial%2Csans-serif%3Bmax-width%3A820px%3Bmargin%3A36px auto%3Bline-height%3A1.38%3Bcolor%3A%23111%7Dh1%7Bfont-size%3A26px%3Bmargin%3A0 0 4px%7Dh2%7Bfont-size%3A18px%3Bmargin%3A22px 0 8px%3Bborder-bottom%3A1px solid %23ddd%3Bpadding-bottom%3A3px%7Dh3%7Bfont-size%3A15px%3Bmargin%3A16px 0 4px%7Dp%2Cli%7Bfont-size%3A11.5px%7Dpre%7Bwhite-space%3Apre-wrap%3Bfont-family%3AArial%2Csans-serif%3Bfont-size%3A11.5px%7D<%2Fstyle><%2Fhead><body><pre>%23 Anton Nazarov%0D%0A**Engineering Manager %2F CTO %2F Systems Architect %2F Tech Lead**%0D%0A%0D%0ABelgrade%2C Serbia  %0D%0APortfolio%3A %5BPortfolio Index%5D\(.%2Fportfolio%2FREADME.md\)%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Profile%0D%0A%0D%0ATechnology leader and systems architect with 18 years of professional experience across startups%2C enterprise%2C and government environments. I build and restructure products and internal systems at the intersection of engineering%2C business%2C and operations%2C with strong ownership of architecture%2C delivery%2C automation%2C team leadership%2C and long-term technical direction.%0D%0A%0D%0AStrongest pattern%3A turning fragmented workflows and weak tooling into scalable systems teams can actually run.%0D%0A%0D%0AI also keep an active eye on product ideas through Serbian IT events and conferences%2C where I look for practical patterns%2C workflow improvements%2C and ways AI-driven dialogue or feedback loops could make services more useful.%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Core Strengths%0D%0A%0D%0A- Engineering leadership and systems architecture%0D%0A- Product delivery from MVP to production%0D%0A- Business process automation and operational restructuring%0D%0A- AI-native development workflows in VS Code%0D%0A- Supabase %2F WeWeb %2F low-code hybrid system design%0D%0A- Cross-functional leadership in uncertain and high-pressure environments%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Selected Experience%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23%23 NeedleBit%2C CTO %2F Systems Architect %2F Product Builder%0D%0A**...on logic%0D%0A- **MetaFox Strengths Explorer%3A** assessment platform with scoring logic%2C PDF reporting%2C peer feedback%2C and admin tooling%0D%0A- **Exit Lead%3A** dual-frontend inspection%2Freporting platform on Glide %2B WeWeb %2B Supabase with automated PDF generation%0D%0A- **Andronyevskaya ERP%3A** self-hosted property support ERP with Telegram Mini App login%2C QR workflows%2C and role-based operations%0D%0A- **AIS MosRazvitie%3A** large-scale government information system with reporting%2C security%2C workflows%2C and interactive maps%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Tech Stack%0D%0A%0D%0A**Architecture %2F Product%3A** system architecture%2C delivery design%2C process optimization%2C stakeholder alignment  %0D%0A**Frontend %2F Builders%3A** WeWeb%2C Bubble%2C Glide%2C Webflow  %0D%0A**Backend %2F Data %2F Automation%3A** Supabase%2C Xano%2C PostgreSQL%2C SQL%2C Supabase Edge Functions%2C n8n%2C Make%2C REST APIs%2C Telegram integrations  %0D%0A**Code %2F AI%3A** JavaScript%2C Python%2C Node.js%2C OpenAI%2C fal.ai%2C AI-assisted development workflows  %0D%0A**Enterprise %2F Legacy%3A** IBM Domino %2F Lotus Notes%2C Active Directory%2C Windows Server%2C Linux%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Education%0D%0A%0D%0A- Bachelor in Management%2C Small Business Management specialization%2C National Institute of Business%2C Moscow%2C 2019%0D%0A- Professional retraining%3A Manager in Information Technologies%2C Humanities Institute%2C Moscow%2C 2019%0D%0A- Applied Informatics in Economics %2F Applied Economics in Informatics coursework%2C Humanities Institute%2C Moscow%2C 2011-2019%3B later transferred before graduation%0D%0A- Background in Accounting and Finance%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Languages%0D%0A%0D%0A- Russian%3A Native%0D%0A- English%3A Fluent%0D%0A- Serbian%3A Fluent%0D%0A%0D%0A%23%23 Additional%0D%0A%0D%0A- Work authorization%3A Serbian sole proprietor \(preduzetnik\)%0D%0A- Experience organizing events up to 10%2C000%2B participants%0D%0A- Built both public-facing products and internal operational systems%0D%0A<%2Fpre><%2Fbody><%2Fhtml>)
